Package: benchrel
Type: Package
Title: Benchmarks as Measurement Instruments: Reliability, Item Selection, and Distribution Shift
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person("Michael", "Hardy", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Analysis code for "Benchmarks as Measurement Instruments:
    Quantifying Signal and Noise for More Efficient AI Evaluations Under
    Distribution Shift". Provides exact, fast estimators for crossed
    model-by-item variance components, generalizability and dependability
    coefficients, the lambda-star-6 item reliability proxy and competing
    item-selection criteria, and empirical reliability curves as items are
    added in a chosen order.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
URL: https://github.com/hardy-education/benchmark_reliability
Depends: R (>= 4.2)
Imports:
    data.table,
    matrixStats,
    stats,
    utils
Suggests:
    fixest,
    ggplot2,
    lme4,
    mirt,
    mokken,
    pcaPP,
    psych,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
